==Battleground==
*3 [[Metal Snache]]s spawn after 5.33 seconds<sup>160f</sup>, delay 3.33~4.67 seconds<sup>100f~140f</sup>.
*4 [[Metal Snache]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 6~8 seconds<sup>180f~240f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Metal Snache]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[THE METAL SLOTH]] spawns as the boss after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Mercury Sloth has 2,400 HP and only takes 1 damage from non-[[Critical Hit]]s, so make sure to bring at least one [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitter]], be it [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Moneko]], [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat]], [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]] or even [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]]. Send out a wave of meatshields and Critical- Hitting units to deal with the enemies, they aren't that troublesome.

If you're later in the game, this stage can be rushed with [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] and [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat.]] Immediately spawn Bullet Train, then one Manic Lion Cat with a Starting Money Up (M) combo to complete the stage. This strategy can be used to farm lucky tickets. If you don't have Bullet Train, Maglev Cat is sufficient.

